.\" robodr-executor(8). Source of truth: the USAGE text and module docs in
.\" crates/robodr-executor/src/bin/robodr-executor.rs, the crate README
.\" (crates/robodr-executor/README.md) and docs/OPERATIONS.md section 6.5.
.\" Keep them in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-EXECUTOR 8 "2026-10-31" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-executor \- carry out RoboDR's reversible response actions (nftables, motion adapters) with a TTL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-executor \-\-config
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-check\-config ]
.br
.B robodr\-executor status \-\-config
.I FILE
.br
.B robodr\-executor revert\-all \-\-config
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-reason
.IR TEXT ]
.br
.B robodr\-executor rearm \-\-config
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-reason
.IR TEXT ]
.br
.B robodr\-executor stop\-cleanup \-\-config
.I FILE
.br
.B robodr\-executor keygen \-\-out
.I FILE
.br
.B robodr\-executor seal\-journal \-\-config
.I FILE
.br
.B robodr\-executor \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B robodr\-executor
is executor v1 of RoboDR: the only process that changes the robot host in
response to a finding. It runs as its own unit and user
.RB ( robodr\-exec ),
holds
.B CAP_NET_ADMIN
and no other capability, and changes exactly one nftables table,
.BR "inet robodr" ,
plus the configured motion adapters.
.PP
It is
.B off by default.
.BR robodr\-agentd (8)
sends it nothing unless
.B executor.enabled
is
.B true
in
.IR agentd.json ;
until then every accepted request stays
.BR recorded_not_executed .
Leave it off for the first field period, and enable it only after the
response policy is OEM-validated and the robot's motion control path,
management and control buses are listed in
.IR executor.json .
.PP
Actions:
.TP
.B isolate_network
drops all traffic in, out and forwarded, except loopback, the management
and uplink allow-list, the robot's control buses, the motion control path,
the robot's DDS discovery and what every host needs (DHCP, path MTU
discovery, IPv6 neighbour and router discovery, MLD). Always with a TTL.
.TP
.B quarantine_node
drops RTPS sent by one participant's GUID prefix, and UDP from and to the
addresses and SPDP locators it was seen at, never inside the motion
control path. Always with a TTL.
.TP
.B record_evidence
runs inside agentd (a signed black-box note); never reverted.
.TP
.BR restrict_motion ", " safe_pause ", " request_safe_state ", " rollback_config
only through the platform
.B motion adapters
of the
.B motion
section of
.I executor.json
(gateway restriction file, Unitree sport speed level, Nav2, ros2_control,
PX4, the site's rollback program), each refused unless the site set its
.BR "oem_validated: true" .
Without a
.B motion
section
.B restrict_motion
is recorded as advisory and the others are refused
.RB ( not_executor_action ).
See the crate README, "Motion adapters", for what each adapter does and
does not revert.
.PP
Every action follows the same sequence: precheck against the executor's
.B own
response policy and configuration (re-read from disk before every order;
an unreadable file refuses), a fresh safety-state check from agentd
(within 500 ms; in observe mode, while the safety system is engaged, or in
an unknown safety state nothing happens), a write-ahead journal entry, one
atomic
.B nft
transaction, a read-back that must match exactly, and the commit with its
deadline. Expiry and reverts run on their own thread. Within a boot the
TTL runs on
.BR CLOCK_BOOTTIME :
a wall-clock step can never make an action outlive its TTL.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
the executor configuration, schema
.B robodr\-executor\-config/v1
(packaged unit:
.IR /etc/robodr/executor.json ;
examples under
.IR /usr/share/doc/robodr/examples/ ).
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
validate the configuration, the response policy and the SOC public keys,
print a summary (robot, morphology, whether the policy is OEM-validated,
allow-list and motion-path entries) and exit; changes nothing.
.TP
.BI \-\-reason " TEXT"
recorded in the journal by
.B revert\-all
and
.BR rearm .
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
.RB ( keygen )
where to write the new link key.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
(none)
run the executor (the systemd unit's
.BR ExecStart= ).
It reconciles the table with its journal, then serves agentd on
.I /run/robodr\-executor/executor.sock
(mode 0660, group
.BR robodr ;
newline-delimited JSON, HMAC-SHA-256 under the link key, timestamp
window and nonce cache; at most 8 connections).
.TP
.B status
print the journal (active, held and reverting actions with their
deadlines); read-only.
.TP
.B revert\-all
revert every active action now (incident over, or before maintenance),
and undo motion actions.
.TP
.B rearm
end an operator's emergency disable, or acknowledge a journal reset, so
orders are accepted again. Works on the journal only, as root, with the
executor
.B stopped
.RB ( "systemctl stop robodr\-executor"
first). agentd's socket has no re-arm: the key it holds cannot lift the
operator's fence.
.TP
.B stop\-cleanup
the unit's
.BR ExecStopPost= :
after any run that did not end in success (crash, watchdog kill, failed
start, start limit) it deletes table
.B inet robodr
and marks the journal, so no rule is left without the process that
enforces its TTL. A clean stop keeps the actions for the next start.
.TP
.B keygen
write a new 32-byte link key (mode 0600, never overwrites) shared by agentd
and the executor through systemd credentials.
.TP
.B seal\-journal
one-time upgrade of an unsealed executor v1 journal to the sealed format,
executor stopped; refused once the journal was ever written sealed.
.SH EMERGENCY DISABLE
.B "nft delete table inet robodr"
as root lifts every RoboDR rule at once. The running executor notices the
missing table, drops its actions without re-applying them, and refuses
every order until an operator runs
.BR rearm .
.SH RESTART AND REBOOT
At start the journal decides: an action still being applied when the
process died is reverted; one whose deadline passed is reverted; one still
active on the same boot is re-applied and verified; one active across a
.B reboot
is
.B held
and re-applied only when agentd supplies a fresh, known, not-engaged
safety state. An unreadable journal, one that fails its seal (edited,
truncated, another key), a missing sealed journal without the package's
.I first\-start
marker, or an older copy put back (agentd's anchor is ahead) is not
believed: the table is deleted, the SOC replay store fenced, and every
order refused until
.BR rearm .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
clean stop, or the command succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
runtime failure (the start path deletes table
.B inet robodr
before it exits).
.TP
.B 2
usage or configuration error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/executor.json
configuration (also motion adapters, Sprint 8).
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/keys/executor.key
link key (0600 root), handed to the unit as
.I /run/credentials/robodr\-executor.service/executor.key
and to agentd with the drop-in example
.IR 30\-executor.conf.example .
.TP
.I /var/lib/robodr/executor/
journal
.RI ( journal.json ,
sealed), SOC replay store
.RI ( soc_nonces.json ),
the
.I first\-start
marker created by the package on first install; 0700
.BR robodr\-exec .
.TP
.I /run/robodr\-executor/executor.sock
agentd's connection.
.SH SYSTEMD UNIT
.B robodr\-executor.service
is installed
.B disabled.
.BR Type=notify ,
.BR WatchdogSec=30s ,
.BR User=robodr\-exec ,
.B CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_NET_ADMIN
only,
.BR ExecStopPost=robodr\-executor " stop\-cleanup".
Kernel requirement: nf_tables (see the modules-load.d example
.IR /usr/share/doc/robodr/examples/modules\-load.d/robodr.conf.example ;
.B robodr\-setup preflight
checks it).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-agentd (8),
.BR robodr\-setup (8),
.BR nft (8),
.I /usr/share/doc/robodr/OPERATIONS.md
(section 6.5),
the crate README
.I crates/robodr\-executor/README.md
in the source tree.
